lógica y puede causar disfagia debido a la pérdida de conectividad funcional en la red de deglución.", "ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON:The \"ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON,\" or Parkinson's disease, is a neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects motor control, leading to difficulties in movement and coordination. This condition can significantly impact various bodily functions, including the ability to interrupt the vagal tone of the esophagus, which is crucial for swallowing. As a result, individuals with Parkinson's disease often experience a high prevalence of swallowing disorders, known as dysphagia, which can increase the risk of malnutrition. Due to these challenges, patients may require nutritional support and specific screening and treatment recommendations to manage their symptoms effectively. Overall, Parkinson's disease is characterized by its profound effects on motor functions and the associated risks of complications related to swallowing and nutrition.", "P. CLAVÉ:P. Clavé is a researcher who has focused on the study of swallowing and has developed methods for evaluating the propulsion forces of the tongue.", "ESCLEROSIS LATERAL AMIOTRÓFICA:Esclerosis lateral amiotrófica (ELA), also known as amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that primarily affects motor neurons. This degeneration leads to significant muscle weakness and can result in dysphagia, or swallowing difficulties, which occur in approximately 60% of patients. As the disease progresses, individuals may experience increased risks of malnutrition due to these swallowing challenges, necessitating specific nutritional interventions and targeted care strategies. The condition is characterized by the gradual loss of motor function, which can ultimately lead to paralysis. Overall, ELA is a complex disease that requires comprehensive management to address both its neurological and nutritional implications.", "ATROFIA MUSCULAR BULBOESPINAL:La atrofia muscular bulboespinal es una condición que causa lesiones en las motoneuronas y afecta la función de deglución.", "PLASTICIDAD NEURONAL:La plasticidad neuronal se refiere a la capacidad del cerebro para reorganizarse y adaptarse, lo que es crucial para la recuperación funcional después de un accidente cerebrovascular.", "NEUROANATOMÍA:", "EES:The upper esophageal sphincter (EES) is a crucial muscular structure that facilitates the opening during the swallowing process, allowing food to pass from the pharynx to the esophagus. It plays a significant role in the swallowing mechanism and can be impacted by various medical conditions, particularly in cases of dysphagia oropharyngeal. The EES is essential for proper swallowing function, and any dysfunction in this area can lead to swallowing disorders.", "P. CALVÉ:P. Calvé es un autor que ha defendido el uso de videofluoroscopia para analizar la respuesta motora orofaríngea y la apertura del EES.", "DIVERTÍCULO DE ZENKER:The \"Divertículo de Zenker\" is a structural issue characterized by the formation of a pharyngeal pouch, which can lead to various swallowing symptoms that are influenced by the size of the diverticulum. This condition is associated with fibrosis of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), which can affect its distensibility. As a result, individuals with Zenker's diverticulum may experience difficulties in swallowing, making it an important esophageal condition to recognize and address.", "ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN:Enfermedad de Crohn, también conocida como Crohn's disease (CD), es un tipo de enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal (EII) que puede afectar cualquier segmento del tracto gastrointestinal, desde la boca hasta el ano. Esta enfermedad se caracteriza por una inflamación discontinua que afecta todas las capas de la pared intestinal, lo que puede llevar a una variedad de síntomas, incluyendo dolor abdominal, diarrea severa, fatiga, pérdida de peso y malnutrición. \n\nLa enfermedad de Crohn es crónica y puede presentar complicaciones como malabsorción de nutrientes, incluyendo la vitamina E, y dificultades para tragar. Además, puede causar problemas en la apertura del esfínter esofágico superior (EES) y tránsito intestinal lento, a menudo asociado con el síndrome de intestino corto. Debido a la naturaleza de la enfermedad, muchos pacientes, especialmente en la población pediátrica, pueden requerir nutrición enteral como parte de su manejo para controlar los síntomas y prevenir la desnutrición. \n\nEn resumen, la enfermedad de Crohn es un trastorno inflamatorio intestinal que provoca una serie de síntomas gastrointestinales y puede tener un impacto significativo en la calidad de vida de quienes la padecen.", "MIOPATÍA POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSIÓN:La miopatía por cuerpos de inclusión es una condición que puede estar relacionada con la disfunción del EES.", "MANOMETRÍA:MANOMETRÍA is a functional diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the pressure and distensibility of the esophageal sphincter (EES) during the act of swallowing. This technique is particularly important for assessing esophageal motility disorders and swallowing function in patients experiencing oropharyngeal dysphagia. By measuring the pressure and patterns of muscle contractions in the esophagus, manometría provides critical insights into the underlying neural or muscular mechanisms, helping to differentiate between primary esophageal obstruction and mechanical obstruction. Often, this procedure is performed alongside impedance testing to enhance diagnostic accuracy."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}